01:02:12.614 --> 01:02:13.746
- Yes.

01:02:13.746 --> 01:02:15.420
- [Audience Member] (murmurs)
here, so there's a gap

01:02:15.420 --> 01:02:18.140
and how do you guys
deal with that pressure,

01:02:18.140 --> 01:02:19.630
that voice in your head that says,

01:02:19.630 --> 01:02:22.270
more content, more this,
more that, bam, bam, bam.

01:02:22.270 --> 01:02:25.630
Because that could be,
you know, a lot of stress

01:02:25.630 --> 01:02:26.463
obviously on you--
- Yeah.

01:02:26.463 --> 01:02:27.296
- [Audience Member] And
you don't move at the end--

01:02:27.296 --> 01:02:29.242
- Yep.
- [Audience Member] Of the day

01:02:29.242 --> 01:02:30.075
because you're always
saying, I should do this,

01:02:30.075 --> 01:02:31.830
I should do that, and then
you're going from A to B

01:02:31.830 --> 01:02:33.471
but nothing doing.

01:02:33.471 --> 01:02:34.304
- I think if you love
doing what you're doing,

01:02:34.304 --> 01:02:35.137
you know what I mean?

01:02:35.137 --> 01:02:36.110
I think that's what it comes down to.

01:02:36.110 --> 01:02:37.490
For me, I only put stuff
out when I feel like it

01:02:37.490 --> 01:02:39.080
and I only hit someone on Instagram

01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:41.740
when I feel like doing
it actually at that time.

01:02:41.740 --> 01:02:43.390
So it's always just based on how I feel,

01:02:43.390 --> 01:02:45.780
like I wanna do what I
do and I'm pretty sure

01:02:45.780 --> 01:02:46.834
and I'll answer for you.

01:02:46.834 --> 01:02:49.500
- That would have been my answer
until somebody very smart,

01:02:49.500 --> 01:02:52.070
friend of mine, Tom Bilyeu,
on a podcast with me,

01:02:52.070 --> 01:02:53.160
looked me dead in the face,

01:02:53.160 --> 01:02:55.760
rocked me, rocked me, 'cause it's true,

01:02:55.760 --> 01:02:57.757
very similar to how you
pegged me with, you know,

01:02:57.757 --> 01:02:59.790
EQ and work ethic, he rocked me.

01:02:59.790 --> 01:03:01.387
He goes, "Do you know
what your superpower is?"

01:03:01.387 --> 01:03:03.130
And I'm already pumped, I'm like, what?

01:03:03.130 --> 01:03:03.963
You know,
(audience laughs)

01:03:03.963 --> 01:03:04.796
like what is it?

01:03:04.796 --> 01:03:05.629
I'm like, what is it?

01:03:05.629 --> 01:03:07.080
And you know, usually in those moments,

01:03:07.080 --> 01:03:09.390
I think he's gonna say
something like work ethic and EQ

01:03:09.390 --> 01:03:12.270
would not surprise me,
that I'm super understand.

01:03:12.270 --> 01:03:14.602
But he looked at me and
goes, "Your superpower,

01:03:14.602 --> 01:03:17.358
and you have this more than
anybody I've ever seen,

01:03:17.358 --> 01:03:21.557
your ability to not judge
yourself is remarkable."

01:03:22.600 --> 01:03:24.040
And that's my answer.

01:03:24.040 --> 01:03:27.040
Every day, my ambition is insane.

01:03:27.040 --> 01:03:28.950
If I decide to sleep all 24 hours

01:03:28.950 --> 01:03:31.523
in the next 24 hours, I'm thrilled.

01:03:34.974 --> 01:03:35.807
- [Man] Yeah.

01:03:35.807 --> 01:03:38.330
- It is the combination of those two.

01:03:38.330 --> 01:03:40.803
I love what I do and if today,

01:03:42.410 --> 01:03:44.773
and this gets into a
singular voice mentality.

01:03:46.030 --> 01:03:47.920
Because I don't think most people

01:03:47.920 --> 01:03:49.470
are actually judging themselves either.

01:03:49.470 --> 01:03:51.360
I think they're taking
the voices of others

01:03:51.360 --> 01:03:54.090
to allow themselves to be judged.

01:03:54.090 --> 01:03:57.010
People are like, Gary,
I hear ya, you know,

01:03:57.010 --> 01:03:58.380
they're like, I get it,
don't listen to others,

01:03:58.380 --> 01:04:01.550
but what if your own voice,
the one in your own head,

01:04:01.550 --> 01:04:03.160
is telling you you suck shit

01:04:03.160 --> 01:04:03.993
or this that and the other thing?

01:04:03.993 --> 01:04:06.550
I'm like, you've taken on
the voice of someone else.

01:04:08.440 --> 01:04:09.740
I really believe that.

01:04:09.740 --> 01:04:13.100
And for some reason, through
self-esteem, serendipity,

01:04:13.100 --> 01:04:15.350
and many other things, I mean,

01:04:15.350 --> 01:04:19.450
I consciously, in third grade,
decided to not try in school.

01:04:19.450 --> 01:04:21.550
Not because I was a normal third grader,

01:04:21.550 --> 01:04:23.810
'cause I definitely wasn't,
it was 'cause I was like,

01:04:23.810 --> 01:04:26.320
fuck, this has nothing to do with my life.

01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:29.120
And I'm gonna start
working on my actual skill.

01:04:29.120 --> 01:04:32.810
And I'm willing to deal with
the judgment of my teachers.

01:04:32.810 --> 01:04:35.010
Do you how not fun it is
to grow up your whole life

01:04:35.010 --> 01:04:38.370
and have all your friends'
parents think you're a loser?

01:04:38.370 --> 01:04:40.070
Because the only framework in society

01:04:40.070 --> 01:04:42.403
at that time is your school grades?

01:04:44.640 --> 01:04:45.940
I think more kids have
to learn to learn how

01:04:45.940 --> 01:04:48.850
to be in a framework of adversity

01:04:48.850 --> 01:04:52.400
because the alternative is
why we have so much sadness,

01:04:52.400 --> 01:04:55.000
which is parents are
creating fake environments,

01:04:55.000 --> 01:04:58.430
kids have no adversity, and
everything's taken care of

01:04:58.430 --> 01:05:00.550
in one way or the other,
whether through financial

01:05:00.550 --> 01:05:03.630
or delusion, and then they
go into the real world,

01:05:03.630 --> 01:05:06.230
and mommy and daddy aren't
around anymore, are they?

01:05:10.808 --> 01:05:11.641
- We're good.

01:05:11.641 --> 01:05:12.474
- Thank you.

01:05:12.474 --> 01:05:13.307
- [Man] Thank you.
- Cheers.

01:05:13.307 --> 01:05:16.307
